	(text "Going with x26 because we don't need RGMII because \ntoo complicated and we don't need 1 gb speeds. \nPlan is running MPEG/MJPEG which is ~15 mbps so chill"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at -138.43 56.896 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
				(color 255 0 15 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "0c2509fe-7d18-421c-b0f8-fa13261563c6")
	)
	(text "1% precision resistor required\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 67.818 134.112 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "0dd5f3a5-fd70-41c4-87aa-926839abda07")
	)
	(text "1. PWR\n	VDDA3V3 = 3.3 V\n	VDDIO = 1.8 V or 3.3 V. (1.8V is strongly considered)\n\n2. CLK\n	A - PHY is RMII leader\n		25MHz OSC to DP. Chip Generates 50MHz RMII CLK\n	B - RMII follower\n		Gen 50MHz CLK from FPGA and feed\n\n3. Magnetics - ???\n	Look into this, there seems to be some fuckery\n	An option would be using a MagJack (RJ45 w/ Magnetics)\n	Pulse HX1198FNL or something as well?\n\n--- Extra ---\n4. RBIAS - 6.49kOhm\n5. CEXT  - 2 nF\n6. PHY RST -  Have this\n7. MDIO / MDC - Route both prob\n8. ESD Prot - Closest to CONN\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at -255.778 120.904 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "1cee58fc-6908-49b5-a877-3d84a1f9883e")
	)
	(text "Mika Notes:"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at -255.524 46.228 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.25)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "2018e995-0d4b-4e9a-ac2f-138807b34c91")
	)
	(text "Karthik Notes:"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at -138.43 47.498 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.25)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "262d9614-abd8-4e4e-a62f-424e04b1e0d5")
	)
	(text "FPGA			PHY\nTXD [1:0] -------> Transmit Data\nTX_EN     -------> Transmit valid / enable\nRXD[1:0]  -------> Recieve Data\nCRS_DV    <------- recieve valid\nREF CLK   <------> Clock\nMDIO/MDC  <------> optional configuration/status"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 143.764 122.174 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "7cd6d3d6-7642-426d-94d6-22f50cef104c")
	)
	(text "Power\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14.224 139.954 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a2aa108d-773d-4acf-9d59-ef9f61f4ea95")
	)
	(text "Just a heads up:\nSs far I have shown 2 options, DP83826I & DP83822I\nSeems that x26 has been chosen, why? (Curious)\n\nBiggest diff that I found is RGMII support\nThis is important because current ZED implements thru RGMII\nWe would be deviating from that using RMII.\nThis is OK, just making sure it is known, and there is\nplan on how this will be implemented\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at -255.27 66.548 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
				(color 255 0 15 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c5397991-4c97-482d-9a57-73eac209f5c2")
	)
	(text "LED 0 indicates activity + Link\nLED 1 is on when link is 100 mbps \nOff when link isnt connected or at 10 mbps\n"
